IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P2-art-15.l4 -- ARTICLE 15 OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679: RIGHT OF ACCESS BY THE DATA SUBJECT (layer 1).
-- Written by P2 (Sonnet 5.5).  Lines 206-219 of eu-gdpr-2016-679-consolidated-20160504.txt (the two heading lines of
-- Article 15 at 206-207 are `inert` headings; the Section 3 heading at 220-221 belongs to Article 16).
-- Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).  Answers: MAYBE BOOLEAN for a right, MAYBE `Duty outcome` for a duty with a
-- gate, a DEONTIC for each regulative rule.
--
-- WHOSE.  Every right below is the data subject's CLAIM against the controller; the controller's duty is its correlative
-- (NOTES, Jural relations).  A right function takes the two role facts `the person is the data subject` and `the body is
-- the controller`; when either is false the grant is not made out (NOTHING: "The data subject shall have the right to
-- obtain from the controller" says nothing of anyone else).
-- ARTICLE 11(2).  "In such cases, Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply": each function of Articles 15 to 20 takes P1's answer
-- `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` (MAYBE BOOLEAN, PLAN-P1.md section 4.2).  JUST TRUE means the article does
-- not apply (a flat negative, JUST FALSE for a right, `the duty does not arise` for a duty); any other answer leaves
-- the article to run.
-- READING A RESULT (NOTES).  NOTHING means the Regulation does not answer on these facts; never read it as no.
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 15(1) item of information` IS ONE OF
    `Art 15(1)(a) the purposes of the processing`
    `Art 15(1)(b) the categories of personal data concerned`
    `Art 15(1)(c) the recipients or categories of recipient to whom the personal data have been or will be disclosed`
    `Art 15(1)(d) the envisaged period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period`
    `Art 15(1)(e) the existence of the right to request rectification or erasure of personal data or restriction of processing, or to object to such processing`
    `Art 15(1)(f) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority`
    `Art 15(1)(g) any available information as to the source of the personal data`
    `Art 15(1)(h) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences`

DECLARE `Art 15 action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 15(1) confirm to the data subject whether or not personal data concerning him or her are being processed, and give access`
    `Art 15(3) provide a copy of the personal data undergoing processing`

§ `Article 15(1): confirmation, access and the information`

-- src:208 | The data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller confirmation as to whether or not personal data concerning him or her are being processed, and, where that is the case, access to the personal data and the following information:
@ref Art 15(1) chapeau: confirmation (src:208)
GIVEN `the person is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(1) the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller confirmation as to whether or not personal data concerning him or her are being processed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the data subject` AND `the body is the controller`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller": a grant to the data subject against the controller, and silent on anyone else (entitlement-named, fork F15-1)
        IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, Article 11(2)): "Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:208 | The data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller confirmation as to whether or not personal data concerning him or her are being processed, and, where that is the case, access to the personal data and the following information:
@ref Art 15(1) chapeau: access (src:208)
GIVEN `the person is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `personal data concerning the data subject are being processed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(1) the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller access to the personal data` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the data subject` AND `the body is the controller`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller": a grant to the data subject against the controller (entitlement-named, fork F15-1)
        IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, Article 11(2)): "Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject"
        IF NOT (`personal data concerning the data subject are being processed`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); an entitlement-named function, fork F15-1): "and, where that is the case, access to the personal data"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:208 | 1. The data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller confirmation as to whether or not personal data concerning him or her are being processed, and, where that is the case, access to the personal data and the following information:
-- src:209 | (a) the purposes of the processing;
-- src:210 | (b) the categories of personal data concerned;
-- src:211 | (c) the recipients or categories of recipient to whom the personal data have been or will be disclosed, in particular recipients in third countries or international organisations;
-- src:212 | (d) where possible, the envisaged period for which the personal data will be stored, or, if not possible, the criteria used to determine that period;
-- src:213 | (e) the existence of the right to request from the controller rectification or erasure of personal data or restriction of processing of personal data concerning the data subject or to object to such processing;
-- src:214 | (f) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority;
-- src:215 | (g) where the personal data are not collected from the data subject, any available information as to their source;
-- src:216 | (h) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4) and, at least in those cases, meaningful information about the logic involved, as well as the significance and the envisaged consequences of such processing for the data subject.
@ref Art 15(1) points (a) to (h): the information (src:208-216)
GIVEN `the person is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `personal data concerning the data subject are being processed` IS A BOOLEAN
      item IS AN `Art 15(1) item of information`
      `the personal data are not collected from the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(1) the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller the following information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the data subject` AND `the body is the controller`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller": a grant to the data subject against the controller (entitlement-named, fork F15-1)
        IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, Article 11(2)): "Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject"
        IF NOT (`personal data concerning the data subject are being processed`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); an entitlement-named function, fork F15-1): "and, where that is the case, access to the personal data and the following information"
        IF item EQUALS `Art 15(1)(g) any available information as to the source of the personal data` AND NOT (`the personal data are not collected from the data subject`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); fork F15-1): "(g) where the personal data are not collected from the data subject, any available information as to their source"
        IF item EQUALS `Art 15(1)(h) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences` AND NOT (`there is automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4)`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(h) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, referred to in Article 22(1) and (4) and, at least in those cases, meaningful information about the logic involved": with no such decision-making there is nothing whose existence can be obtained, and the text does not say no (fork F13-3)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    -- (c) "in particular recipients in third countries or international organisations": an example; not read.  (d) "where possible, the envisaged period ..., or, if not possible, the criteria": the item is either the period or the criteria, so a caller states the item once.

-- src:217 | 2. Where personal data are transferred to a third country or to an international organisation, the data subject shall have the right to be informed of the appropriate safeguards pursuant to Article 46 relating to the transfer.
@ref Art 15(2) (src:217)
GIVEN `the person is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `personal data are transferred to a third country or to an international organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(2) the data subject has the right to be informed of the appropriate safeguards pursuant to Article 46 relating to the transfer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the data subject` AND `the body is the controller`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the data subject shall have the right to be informed": a grant to the data subject (the party bound is named only by Article 15(1); entitlement-named, fork F15-1)
        IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, Article 11(2)): "Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject"
        IF NOT (`personal data are transferred to a third country or to an international organisation`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b); an entitlement-named function, fork F15-1): "Where personal data are transferred to a third country or to an international organisation, the data subject shall have the right to be informed"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

GIVEN `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 15 action`
`Art 15(1) the controller must confirm whether personal data concerning the data subject are being processed and give access` MEANS
    IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 15(1) confirm to the data subject whether or not personal data concerning him or her are being processed, and give access`
    -- the correlative of the right: the text names the controller and the act, and no time limit or consequence (Article 12(3) fixes when the controller must answer the request, not when the act must be done; NOTES, Rules with no breach path)

§ `Article 15(3) and (4): the copy`

-- src:218 | The controller shall provide a copy of the personal data undergoing processing.
@ref Art 15(3) first sentence (src:218)
GIVEN `personal data are undergoing processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller has provided a copy of the personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 15(3) the controller provides a copy of the personal data undergoing processing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, Article 11(2)): "Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject"
        IF NOT (`personal data are undergoing processing`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a copy of the personal data undergoing processing": with no personal data undergoing processing there is nothing to copy, and the text does not say no
        IF `the controller has provided a copy of the personal data`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "The controller shall provide a copy of the personal data undergoing processing"

GIVEN `personal data are undergoing processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 15 action`
`Art 15(3) the controller must provide a copy of the personal data undergoing processing` MEANS
    IF `personal data are undergoing processing` AND NOT (`Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 15(3) provide a copy of the personal data undergoing processing`
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- no time limit and no consequence is stated (NOTES, Rules with no breach path)

-- src:218 | For any further copies requested by the data subject, the controller may charge a reasonable fee based on administrative costs.
@ref Art 15(3) second sentence (src:218)
GIVEN `the data subject has requested a further copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee is reasonable and based on administrative costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(3) the controller may charge a reasonable fee based on administrative costs for any further copies requested by the data subject` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the data subject has requested a further copy`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For any further copies requested by the data subject": a request for the first copy is outside the sentence (Article 12(5) says the first is free of charge), and the sentence has no gate word
        IF `the fee is reasonable and based on administrative costs`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a reasonable fee based on administrative costs": a fee outside that limit is outside the grant, and the text does not say no to it in its own words

-- src:218 | Where the data subject makes the request by electronic means, and unless otherwise requested by the data subject, the information shall be provided in a commonly used electronic form.
@ref Art 15(3) third sentence (src:218)
GIVEN `the data subject makes the request by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject has requested otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is provided in a commonly used electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 15(3) the information is provided in a commonly used electronic form where the request is made by electronic means` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the data subject makes the request by electronic means`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b)): "Where the data subject makes the request by electronic means"
        IF `the data subject has requested otherwise`
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "unless"): "and unless otherwise requested by the data subject"
        IF `the information is provided in a commonly used electronic form`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "the information shall be provided in a commonly used electronic form"

-- src:219 | 4. The right to obtain a copy referred to in paragraph 3 shall not adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others.
@ref Art 15(4) (src:219)
GIVEN `the copy would adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 15(4) the right to obtain a copy is limited because the copy would adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others` MEANS
    IF `the copy would adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a flat negative; JUST TRUE here means the limit applies): "shall not adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others"; JUST TRUE here means the limit applies
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others": where the copy has no such effect the limit is not engaged and the paragraph is silent
